Guidelines for Programmatic Management of TB Preventive Treatment in India 2021
39
The following are the salient features of the integrated algorithm:
• Once a DR-TB patient has been identified, all household contacts are counselled, screened
and evaluated to rule out active TB;
• NAAT is used upfront among contacts with symptoms or abnormal chest X-ray to diagnose
TB;
• If the result is MTB detected with no resistance, the treatment for DS-TB is initiated;
• If the result is MTB detected with H and/or R resistance, manage as per DR-TB guidelines;
• If the result is MTB not detected, in HHC <5 years, assess for TPT and check for any
contraindications;
• If the result is MTB not detected, in HHC >5 years of age with TBI test positive or unavailable
and chest X-ray is normal or unavailable check for any contraindications;
