9.4.2 Clinical monitoring
• All patients receiving TPT should be evaluated at least monthly or at every contact by the
doctor of HF (including CHO) with the person on TPT for the following:
►
►Assess adherence and provide necessary support. Any interruption in treatment
should be discussed with the person on treatment and her/his treatment supporter and
interventions to address problems in adherence should be instituted;
►
►Signs and symptoms of TB disease (“breakthrough” or missed diagnosis at start of
TPT);
►
►Adverse reactions (type, onset and duration, severity);
►
►Other co-morbid diseases during TPT, such as COVID-19, malaria etc;
